  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Uplift Education Fund; Philippines</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Due to COVID-19, all public schools in the Philippines were closed for over 750 consecutive days - the longest educational shutdown in the world.  Of the 3,625 public schools across the Philippines, less than 15% have connectivity or computers for students to access learning resources, and over 23 million children are in learning poverty. This has contributed to an education emergency threatening an entire generation that might be forced to give up on their basic right to quality education.</narrative>
  </description>
